{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 6, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)\npoles of 1/(z - 1)^2:\n  none in |Re z|, |Im z| <= 7\n  numerically: zeros of 1/f by Newton's method from a grid in |Re z|, |Im z| <= 7; orders from the growth of |f| on circles of radius 1e-2..1e-4, residues by circle integrals\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 6, "ok": true, "cmd": "poles", "ucas": "poles 1/(z-1)^2", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "poles", "var": "z", "poles": []}, "notes": [{"kind": "assumed", "text": "z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "numeric", "text": "zeros of 1/f by Newton's method from a grid"}, "files": [], "text": "  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)\npoles of 1/(z - 1)^2:\n  none in |Re z|, |Im z| <= 7\n  numerically: zeros of 1/f by Newton's method from a grid in |Re z|, |Im z| <= 7; orders from the growth of |f| on circles of radius 1e-2..1e-4, residues by circle integrals\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 7, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)\npoles of 1/((z - 1)^2*(z + 2)):\n    z = -2  order 1, residue 1/9\n  numerically: zeros of 1/f by Newton's method from a grid in |Re z|, |Im z| <= 7; orders from the growth of |f| on circles of radius 1e-2..1e-4, residues by circle integrals\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 7, "ok": true, "cmd": "poles", "ucas": "poles 1/((z-1)^2*(z+2))", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "poles", "var": "z", "poles": [{"at": "-2", "order": 1, "residue": "1/9"}]}, "notes": [{"kind": "assumed", "text": "z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "numeric", "text": "zeros of 1/f by Newton's method from a grid"}, "files": [], "text": "  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)\npoles of 1/((z - 1)^2*(z + 2)):\n    z = -2  order 1, residue 1/9\n  numerically: zeros of 1/f by Newton's method from a grid in |Re z|, |Im z| <= 7; orders from the growth of |f| on circles of radius 1e-2..1e-4, residues by circle integrals\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 8, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)\nresidue of 1/((z - 1)^2*(z + 2)) at z = 1:\n  = -0.1111111111\n  a pole of order 2 (|f| grows like |z - a|^-2)\n  computed as (1/(2 pi i)) times the integral of 1/((z - 1)^2*(z + 2)) on |z - a| = 0.01 and 0.005 (512 points each): they agree\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 8, "ok": true, "cmd": "residue", "ucas": "residue 1/((z-1)^2*(z+2)) at 1", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "residue", "var": "z", "at": "1", "found": true, "residue": "-0.1111111111", "re": -0.11111111111090971, "im": 0, "singularity": "pole", "order": 2}, "notes": [{"kind": "assumed", "text": "z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "circle_integrals", "points": 1024, "passed": true, "text": "radius 0.01 and 0.005 agree"}], "files": [], "text": "  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)\nresidue of 1/((z - 1)^2*(z + 2)) at z = 1:\n  = -0.1111111111\n  a pole of order 2 (|f| grows like |z - a|^-2)\n  computed as (1/(2 pi i)) times the integral of 1/((z - 1)^2*(z + 2)) on |z - a| = 0.01 and 0.005 (512 points each): they agree\n"}, "isError": false}}
